trufflehog --no-update git file://. --since-commit HEAD --results=verified,unknown --fail --trust-local-git-config && zizmor .github/workflows && npm run lint && npm run spellcheck && npm run typecheck && npm run validate && npm run test

# `npm run build` used to run here, conditionally, whenever a staged path could
# affect build output. It prerenders all 335 route pages and takes ~9 minutes,
# which is why the condition existed at all - and why `--no-verify` became the
# habit on any commit in a series, which quietly cost us the other checks too.
#
# It is no longer worth that. The .github/workflows/checks.yml workflow now runs
# lint, typecheck and the data validators on every push and PR, and the Azure
# deploy workflow still runs the full `npm run build` (via Oryx) on the way to a
# preview environment - so a prerender failure is caught before merge either
# way, ~4 minutes into a job nobody is waiting on, rather than ~9 minutes into a
# commit somebody is.
#
# What stays here is everything that is fast enough to never be worth skipping:
# secret scanning, workflow auditing, lint, spellcheck, typecheck, the
# validators and the vitest unit suite (~2s) - about 25 seconds of work plus
# trufflehog.
